Session#How to create the next handoff#Structure#{7}":[119,119],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Structure#{8}":[120,120],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Structure#{9}":[121,122],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules":[123,130],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules#{1}":[125,125],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules#{2}":[126,126],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules#{3}":[127,127],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules#{4}":[128,128],"#April 28th — BS Closure Session#How to create the next handoff#Consolidation rules#{5}":[129,130]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"type":"session-handoff","date":"2026-04-28","topic":"Made the forecast balance sheet balance to $0 across all 3 tickers (PEP/PG/CELH) by implementing Path B closure — BS-driven CF where every BS row's delta is absorbed by a CF entry. Diagnosed root causes (BS+CF forecast independently → identity drift), introduced RESIDUAL_PLUG, library-declared cf_delta_target, APIC/AOCI rollforwards capturing SBC + FX equity offsets, ZERO defaults for non-anchor CF rows, dynamic FORECAST_LABELS, annual→QTR row mirror in model-write, forecast cell formatting carried from historicals. Cleaned up stale workbooks; one canonical xlsx per ticker.","tags":["#session","#bs-closure","#path-b","#residual-plug","#cf-delta-target","#forecast-formatting"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Sessions/CELH Model/Handoffs/April 28th BS Closure Session.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":"kl4r1j","at":1777392829086},"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.02816746,-0.05186158,-0.0130852,-0.02898887,-0.00463604,-0.0319464,-0.03620369,-0.01460627,0.05361418,-0.03320223,-0.00814599,0.0060820